#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#Advanced users can define torques applied to the wheels and reacted at the unsprung mass to simulate in-wheel motors such as those used in some hybrid powertrains.
#
#The simple logic used here to define the drive torques can be replaced with more detailed descriptions of hybrid components and controllers using VS Commands, Simulink, LabVIEW, or other modeling packages linked to CarSim through the API.
#
#Other import variables are available for drive torques and brake torques. Drive torques are applied to the wheels with reactions at the unsprung mass for independent suspensions and the sprung mass for solid axles. Brake torques are applied to the wheels with reactions at the unsprung mass and always oppose the direction of wheel rotation.
#
#For a complete list of import variables, please see the drop-down menu in the lower-right corner of the Run Control screen. Select "Imports into math model" (text or Excel), then click the "View" button next to that drop-down list to view the file.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

